Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:04.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This is CABINET,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.55,0:00:08.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a framework for table question answering published at ICLR 2024 by researchers at Adobe's
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.60,0:00:12.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}MDSR Lab together with IIT Kharagpur and IIT Roorkee.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.65,0:00:16.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Large language models reason over tables,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.70,0:00:20.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but only a few cells usually matter for any given question,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.76,0:00:24.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the irrelevant cells act as noise that hurts accuracy.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.81,0:00:28.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}CABINET tackles this by teaching the model to focus on relevant table content and suppress the rest,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.86,0:00:32.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}rather than deleting parts of the table outright.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.91,0:00:36.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It sets new state of the art on three challenging table QA benchmarks.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.26,0:00:40.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Tables organize information across rows and columns,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.46,0:00:45.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but for any single question only a small number of cells actually contain the answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.70,0:00:49.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Everything else is irrelevant to that question and behaves like noise.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.01,0:00:54.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Large language models are known to be susceptible to such distracting information,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.06,0:00:57.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so their table reasoning degrades,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.15,0:01:02.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the problem gets worse as tables grow larger and carry even more irrelevant content.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.57,0:01:05.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}CABINET is built to address exactly this vulnerability.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.26,0:01:10.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A natural way to reduce noise is to shrink the table before answering,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.56,0:01:15.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and methods like DATER do this by decomposing the table into a smaller sub-table.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.55,0:01:21.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The trouble is that hard decomposition is unforgiving: if the wrong sub-table is extracted,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.14,0:01:27.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}useful information is permanently lost and the reasoner answers incorrectly with no way to recover.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.23,0:01:34.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}CABINET argues for a softer approach that weighs relevant parts higher without ever explicitly removing content,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.12,0:01:40.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so the answering model retains access to the whole table while being steered toward what matters.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.38,0:01:44.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The paper contributes CABINET, short for Content Relevance-Based Noise Reduction.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.33,0:01:48.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It has two cooperating parts.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.29,0:01:52.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.24,0:01:56.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}an Unsupervised Relevance Scorer assigns a soft relevance weight to every table token
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.20,0:02:00.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and is trained differentiably alongside the question-answering model.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.15,0:02:04.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.11,0:02:07.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a weakly-supervised module generates a parsing statement describing which rows and columns matter,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.06,0:02:11.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}then highlights the corresponding cells to produce a cell-based relevance signal.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.02,0:02:15.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Together they let the model focus without discarding content,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.98,0:02:19.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and they deliver new state of the art on three benchmarks along with stronger robustness to noise and to large tables.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.23,0:02:22.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}CABINET works in a sequence of steps.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.46,0:02:29.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The table is flattened into a linear string with header and row markers and embedded together with the question.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.20,0:02:32.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}An Unsupervised Relevance Scorer, a transformer encoder,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.57,0:02:36.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}reads this and predicts a relevance score for each table token.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.37,0:02:40.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Because there are no ground-truth annotations for which cells are relevant,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.88,0:02:45.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}relevance is treated as a latent variable estimated through variational inference,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.82,0:02:51.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the encoder's representation space is shaped by a clustering loss that groups tokens
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.12,0:02:52.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}into relevant and non-relevant,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.99,0:02:56.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a separation loss that pushes the two cluster centroids apart,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.72,0:03:02.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and a sparsification loss that drives irrelevant scores toward zero and relevant scores toward one.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.68,0:03:06.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Each table token's embedding is multiplied by its relevance score,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.65,0:03:10.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so noisy cells are softly suppressed rather than deleted,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.09,0:03:15.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the whole system trains end-to-end through the answer-generation cross-entropy loss.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.39,0:03:18.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In parallel a weakly-supervised Parsing Statement Generator,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.00,0:03:24.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a fine-tuned Flan T5-xl bootstrapped from only about three hundred manual annotations,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.18,0:03:28.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}writes a natural-language description of which rows and columns are relevant,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.81,0:03:32.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and a cell highlighter turns that into a cell-based relevance score.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.91,0:03:39.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The unsupervised and cell-based scores are linearly combined into the final weight applied to the table.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.47,0:03:44.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}CABINET is evaluated on three challenging table question-answering benchmarks.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.58,0:03:46.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}WikiTableQuestions, or WikiTQ,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.54,0:03:54.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}requires compositional reasoning over tables and uses short one-to-two-word answers scored by exact-match accuracy.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.08,0:03:56.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}WikiSQL similarly uses exact-match accuracy.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.96,0:04:00.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}FeTaQA asks for long, free-form descriptive answers,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.36,0:04:02.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which are scored with Sacre-BLEU.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.52,0:04:08.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors additionally release a small dataset of about three hundred manually written
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.29,0:04:13.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}parsing statements used to bootstrap the weakly-supervised cell-highlighting module.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.09,0:04:18.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}CABINET establishes new state of the art on all three benchmarks.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.63,0:04:23.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On WikiTQ it reaches sixty-nine point one percent exact-match accuracy,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.58,0:04:29.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}outperforming the strongest baseline in each category, including OmniTab, DATER,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.17,0:04:33.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and fine-tuned Flan T5-xl by six point four, three point two,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.42,0:04:36.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and four point seven absolute percentage points,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.77,0:04:41.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and it beats much larger GPT-3 and Codex based in-context learning methods.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.01,0:04:45.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On FeTaQA it achieves a Sacre-BLEU of forty point five,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.85,0:04:50.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and on WikiSQL it reaches eighty-nine point five percent accuracy,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.45,0:04:52.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}pushing past the previous best.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.62,0:04:58.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Notably all of this is achieved with a compact five hundred sixty million parameter model.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.20,0:05:01.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Ablations confirm both components are needed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.02,0:05:06.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}For the Unsupervised Relevance Scorer, applying clustering, centroid-separation,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.02,0:05:13.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and sparsification losses together lifts WikiTQ accuracy from sixty point eight to sixty-five point six percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.03,0:05:16.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}whereas any subset gives little benefit,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.53,0:05:19.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}showing the three losses only help in combination.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.66,0:05:21.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}For the two relevance signals,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.54,0:05:26.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}fusing the unsupervised score at weight zero point seven with the cell-based score at
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.86,0:05:28.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}weight zero point three is optimal,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.05,0:05:31.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}giving sixty-nine point one percent on WikiTQ.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.92,0:05:37.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Relying on the cell-based signal alone collapses accuracy to thirty-seven point six percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.68,0:05:44.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}confirming the unsupervised scorer is the primary driver and the parsing-statement module is a complementary aid.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.05,0:05:49.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The headline numbers are sixty-nine point one percent accuracy on WikiTQ,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.79,0:05:52.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a Sacre-BLEU of forty point five on FeTaQA,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.59,0:05:56.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and eighty-nine point five percent accuracy on WikiSQL,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.16,0:06:01.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}each a new state of the art achieved with just five hundred sixty million parameters.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.69,0:06:02.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Beyond raw accuracy,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.99,0:06:08.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}CABINET is markedly more robust: under table perturbations such as row and column permutation
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.03,0:06:12.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and cell replacement it degrades far less than baselines,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.74,0:06:18.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with roughly an eleven and a half percent smaller performance drop than OmniTab on WikiTQ,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.59,0:06:21.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and it holds its advantage as tables grow larger.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.07,0:06:27.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The core lesson of CABINET is that you do not need to cut a table down to answer questions about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.97,0:06:32.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}By softly weighting every cell according to a learned relevance score,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.11,0:06:36.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}instead of hard-decomposing the table and risking the loss of useful information,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.89,0:06:41.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the model keeps full access to the data while being steered toward what matters.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.62,0:06:47.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Pairing a differentiable unsupervised relevance scorer with a weakly-supervised parsing-statement
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.34,0:06:51.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}cell highlighter yields both higher accuracy and greater robustness to noise,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.89,0:06:58.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}setting new state of the art on three table QA benchmarks with a compact five hundred sixty million parameter model.
